Author: Danny Milosavljevic <dannym@friendly-machines.com>
Date: 2026-05-07
Subject: Make TPaiProp.Create an explicit override
License: expat

TPaiProp.Create has no live polymorphic construction path in the 3.0.4
compiler sources: no descendants of TPaiProp, no class-of TPaiProp or
TAoptBase use, and no non-comment call through TAoptBase.Create.

In Pascal, "reintroduce" intentionally hides the inherited virtual
TAoptBase.Create slot.  C++ cannot express a same-signature derived method
that does not override an inherited virtual.  Mark this constructor as an
explicit override so the Pascal source matches the C++ dispatch semantics
that tp2cc can emit.

--- a/compiler/aoptobj.pas
+++ b/compiler/aoptobj.pas
@@ -133,7 +133,7 @@ Unit AoptObj;
         { can this instruction be removed? }
         CanBeRemoved: Boolean;
 
-        Constructor create; reintroduce;
+        Constructor create; override;
 
         { checks the whole sequence of which (so regs[which].StartMod and and  }
         { the next NrOfMods Tai objects) to see whether Reg is used somewhere, }
